 36AR c  Observation of emission of |a cluster from the breakup of the target   
 36AR c  50 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca beam produced at the GANIL facility. A          
 36AR2c  self-supported 0.2-mg/cm{+2} natural Ca target. Ejectiles identified in
 36AR3c  the focal plane of the SPEG spectrometer in coincidence with the       
 36AR4c  light charged particles detected in the INDRA 4|p array of 240 CsI(Tl) 
 36AR5c  detectors. FWHM=350 keV. Measured E|a and |a(|q) from |a-emission      
 36AR6c  through the nuclear breakup. Deduced missing energy spectrum of        
 36AR7c  {+36}Ar in the excitation range of 20-50 MeV                           
